{ Editorial study excerpt from source game 58. Result * means this chapter ends before the game; it does not change the source result. Annotations and analysis variations are editorial, not verbatim speech. Eric's Caro-Kann Speedrun, 1200-1400 ELO - watch this game from about 1:02:20: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HI0Q1obUbXA&list=PLUjxDD7HNNTjVEZ_1I8E28uav9t_ltDKX&t=3740s } 1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. Nf3 e6 5. Nh4 { The knight attacks Bf5 but is undefended on the d8-h4 diagonal. 5...Qxh4 wins it; 6.g3 Qe4+ forks king and rook. } 5... Qxh4 6. g3 Qe4+ 7. Be2 Qxh1+ { Played continuation: the queen wins the knight, then forks king and rook. White could defend more stubbornly than 6.g3. } *
